cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite this repository and the accompanying manuscript."
title: "Steam Tag Hybridization: measuring category spanning as distance rather than count"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible research codebase for quantifying tag hybridization in indie
  video games on Steam. It (i) audits an existing count-based pipeline for
  reproducibility, and (ii) replaces the count index with dispersion-based
  measures built on a continuous tag embedding: coherence (concentration across
  tag domains) and spanning distance (how far apart the spanned domains are).
  Reports a null-model test showing that the Steam tag network has genuine
  community structure (z = 118.5 against a degree-preserving null), evidence
  that hard partitions of that structure are fragile, and the finding that
  partition-free tag-level distance is the robust measure.
